  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1147 PM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nRain Chances...Shower activity has been pretty unimpressive along\nthe front so far this evening across MN and western WI, but still\nexpecting rain shower activity to develop/spread into portions of\ncentral and northern WI overnight into Sunday morning. Then as \nthe front sinks south, a weak area of FGEN could keep some showers\ngoing for parts of the afternoon/evening, with some CAMs \ncontinuing to suggest isolated to scattered light shower activity.\nStill some uncertainty to how persistent this this activity will \nbe and if it will last into Sunday evening. Any rain would be on\nthe lighter side, with under a quarter inch where it does rain\nexpected. Will continue with rain chances of 15-40% to cover the \nshower activity. As the front lift back north late Monday into \nTuesday, another chance (30-55%) for showers will move into mainly\ncentral and north-central WI. Additional chances for rain return \nlate Tuesday night and Wednesday, and then again late Thursday \nnight into next weekend as two systems trek across the region.\nCurrent thinking remains that the heavier and more persistent \nrainfall will remain northwest of the area through Wednesday, \ncloser to the low pressure system and stronger shortwaves.\n\nTemperatures...another mild day is in store across east-central WI\non Sunday, with highs remaining around 70 degrees. However, behind\nthe frontal boundary, temps will be ~15 cooler than Saturday, with\nhighs in the mid to upper 50s. As the boundary shifts to our\nsouth, a cool day is expected on Monday with highs in the upper\n40s and 50s. The cool down will be very short-lived, as highs will\nrebound 5-10 degrees on Tuesday then back into the mid 60s to low\n70s on Wednesday. Above normal temps remain likely Thursday into\nnext weekend, with highs mainly in the 60s to near 70.",
